From 195eb2578c34c974dc24d73f08595425f931a32b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tangelo Dev <tangelo-dev@noreply.invalid>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 01:36:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] boss: real SpotPass storage registration
 (SetStorageInfo/GetStorageInfo)

HLE BOSS answered GetStorageInfo with 0 and ignored SetStorageInfo, so a
title that had registered its SpotPass storage (e.g. Disney Magical World
with online LLE on) found none with LLE off and showed "The SD card is
not readable".

- BOSS_A.db (the BOSS module's per-title database, layout from 3dbrew
  "BOSS Savegame") is now read when a session is initialized, so storage
  registered by the real module is picked up.
- SetStorageInfo stores the extdata ID, size and media type and writes
  them to the title's BOSS_A.db entry (updating it, or appending a new
  entry), so the registration survives restarts and is shared with LLE.
- GetStorageInfo returns the registered size; UnregisterStorage clears it.
- The registered extdata ID is used to find downloaded SpotPass files.
- DeleteNsData deletes the matching file from the SpotPass extdata
  (unknown IDs still succeed, as before).
- OnlineService serialization gets version 1 for the new fields; older
  savestates still load.

Tests: src/tests/core/hle/service/boss_storage.cpp.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
